<dc:title>Benjamin Banneker</dc:title>
<dc:description>Banneker was a free African American surveyor, mathematician, and almanac author from Maryland. In 1791, he assisted &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/105&quot;&gt;Andrew Ellicott &lt;/a&gt;with a survey of the boundaries of the District of Columbia. Among his duties on the survey, &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/514&quot;&gt;Banneker&lt;/a&gt; operated the astronomical equipment which helped the surveyors determine their exact location.</dc:description>
